    "final_message": "The red acceptance test is written and committed (74910d6), and it fails at the story's \"then\" as intended.\n\n**The spec** (`<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v8-opus-low/spec.toml`):\n- **Names:** app `story_drafting`, bounded context `drafting`, aggregate `Jtbd` with identity `jtbd_id` and one field, `job`.\n- **Operations:** the client submits with `submit_jtbd` and reads with `check_status`. The workflow operation is `work_through_jtbd` and the one action is `record_submission`. The collection is `jtbds`.\n- **Calling mode:** I chose `\"start\"`, because this workflow will eventually wait for the developer's pick. Submitting answers once the workflow has started, and the test retries its read for up to 30 seconds.\n\n**The test:** `TestSubmittingAJtbd::test_a_jtbd_checked_right_after_submitting_is_drafting` in `<repo>/story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`. It uses only the running host:\n1. It sends `POST /jtbds` with a random `job` and expects 201 and a `jtbd_id`.\n2. It polls `GET /jtbds/{jtbd_id}` until that answers 200.\n3. It checks that the read gives back the submitted `jtbd_id` and `job`.\n4. It asserts `check_status.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"` \u2014 the \"then\".\n\n**Verify run:** tessercheck, `mypy --strict` and the non-root tests all passed. The host was served and its Restate endpoint registered. Only the root tier failed, at line 44:\n\n```\n>       assert check_status.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"\nE       AssertionError: assert None == 'drafting'\nE        ... = {'jtbd_id': '04ec6703-...', 'job': 'design a checkout then build it'}.get\n```\n\nSubmitting and reading back both work, so it fails only because the read doesn't answer a step yet, which is the missing behaviour."
